F7.1 ac=scope at=src/superclaude/skills/sc-pr-submit-protocol/refs/finding-verify.md:35 anchor=src/superclaude/skills/sc-pr-submit-protocol/refs/finding-verify.md:10 chk=n,y,y,n family=readonly-wave-push fix=Delete "so commit and push the PR head before relying on it". Keep only the brief's note: it sees pushed commits only, and unpushed changes use codegraph or Grep. covers="a note that only pushed commits are visible": The added text tells the agent to commit and push the PR head during C3a grounding. That instruction is new: the brief asked only for a note that just pushed commits are visible. The same file says at :9-11 that this wave "is **read-only** ... It performs NO version-control mutation". The new instruction makes that claim false. An agent that follows it would push to the remote from a wave declared read-only, outside the task's declared outputs. It also conflicts with the next sentence at :36, which sends unpushed changes to codegraph or Grep.

F7.2 ac=scope at=src/superclaude/skills/sc-pr-submit-protocol/refs/finding-verify.md:34 anchor=src/superclaude/skills/sc-pr-submit-protocol/refs/finding-verify.md:10 chk=n,y,n,n family=readonly-wave-shell-token fix=Change the NFR-6 note at :9-11 so it allows the read-only `git remote get-url origin` lookup, or move that lookup out of this ref. The file then stays truthful. (tests/pr_submit/test_static_grep.py CORE_PURE_FILES does not include this file, so no test catches it.): The note at :10-11 says the wave "contains no shell command tokens". The AUG phrase added at :34 brings in the shell command `git remote get-url origin`, so that claim is now false. The mandated phrase forces the token, but the file's own claim was not updated to match.

F7.3 ac=scope at=src/superclaude/skills/sc-auggie-review-protocol/SKILL.md:225 anchor="AUG phrase (full form, verbatim)" chk=n,n,n,y family=aug-phrase-verbatim fix=Close the parenthetical after the `mcp__auggie__codebase-retrieval` clause and keep the sentence as given: "... call `mcp__auggie__codebase-retrieval`. For uncommitted or unpushed changes use codegraph or Grep." Or restructure the bullet so the full phrase stands as its own sentence. covers="AUG phrase (full form, verbatim)": The full phrase at :225 is nested inside a parenthetical, and ". For uncommitted" was rewritten to "; for uncommitted". So the phrase is not verbatim. The meaning is unchanged; only the wording differs.
